# 8. TMF Return Features

## Log Return

\[
r_t =
\ln\left(\frac{P_t}{P_{t-1}}\right)
\]

Potential variables:

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `tmf_ret_5m` | Previous 5-minute return |
| `tmf_ret_15m` | Trailing 15-minute return |
| `tmf_ret_30m` | Trailing 30-minute return |
| `tmf_ret_60m` | Trailing 60-minute return |
| `tmf_ret_120m` | Trailing 120-minute return |

All trailing returns must use observations available at or before timestamp `t`.

---

# 9. TMF Forward Targets

Forward returns are dependent variables and must never appear as model predictors.

General definition:

\[
R_{t,h}
=
\frac{P_{t+h}}{P_t}-1
\]

Targets:

| Variable | Horizon | Role |
|---|---:|---|
| `tmf_fwd_15m` | 15m | Target |
| `tmf_fwd_30m` | 30m | Target |
| `tmf_fwd_60m` | 60m | Primary target |
| `tmf_fwd_120m` | 120m | Target |

These variables are explicitly future information.

They may only appear on the dependent-variable side of predictive models.

---

# 10. TMF Direction Targets

Classification models may use binary targets.

Example:

\[
Direction_{60m}
=
\begin{cases}
1 & R_{t+60}>0\\
0 & R_{t+60}\leq0
\end{cases}
\]

Variables:

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `tmf_dir_15m` | 1 if 15m forward return > 0 |
| `tmf_dir_30m` | 1 if 30m forward return > 0 |
| `tmf_dir_60m` | 1 if 60m forward return > 0 |
| `tmf_dir_120m` | 1 if 120m forward return > 0 |

---

# 11. TMF VWAP Features

Intraday VWAP:

\[
VWAP_t =
\frac{\sum Price_iVolume_i}
{\sum Volume_i}
\]

Variables:

| Variable | Unit | Description |
|---|---:|---|
| `tmf_vwap` | USD | Session VWAP through timestamp t |
| `tmf_vwap_distance` | % | Distance from VWAP |

VWAP distance:

\[
VWAPDistance_t=
\frac{P_t-VWAP_t}{VWAP_t}
\]

VWAP must only use observations from the current session up to timestamp `t`.

