# 27. Macroeconomic Surprise Variables

Basic surprise:

\[
Surprise=Actual-Consensus
\]

Potential fields:

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `macro_surprise_raw` | Actual minus consensus |
| `macro_surprise_z` | Standardized surprise |
| `macro_positive_surprise` | Positive surprise indicator |
| `macro_negative_surprise` | Negative surprise indicator |

Standardized surprise:

\[
Z=
\frac{Actual-Consensus}
{\sigma_{historical\ surprises}}
\]

Historical standard deviation must use only information available prior to the event.

Different macroeconomic releases should not be combined blindly because their units and economic meanings differ.

