# 40. Leakage Classification

Each field should eventually be assigned one of three classifications.

## SAFE

Known at timestamp `t`.

Example:

```text
ust30y_chg_15m
```

assuming the underlying observations existed at or before `t`.

## TARGET ONLY

Contains future information and may only be used as a dependent variable.

Example:

```text
tmf_fwd_60m
```

## CONDITIONAL

Safe only under specific timing assumptions.

Example:

```text
macro_consensus
```

A consensus forecast is safe if it represents the consensus available before the release.

A subsequently revised historical consensus database could create leakage if revisions are not timestamped.

